<section class="page-section page-section-grey">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="gw-prose">
      <h2 class="section-title">What does a groundworks contractor in Surrey do?</h2>
      <p class="gw-answer">{A_WHAT}</p>

      <p>Groundworks sit at the front of the construction programme. Nothing above ground starts until the site is cleared, formation levels are correct and the substructure is in place, so the groundworks contractor is usually the first main trade on site and sets the timetable for everyone who follows.</p>

      <p>The work is governed by paperwork rather than judgement on the day. Drawings define the footprint, the engineer specifies the foundation type and reinforcement, and agreed datum and formation levels control the depth of every dig. Building control signs off the below-ground elements before they are covered up, so a contractor who works from approved drawings and records what was built is far easier to coordinate with.</p>

      <p>It also helps to be clear where groundworks stop and other disciplines begin. <a href="/demolition">Demolition and site clearance</a> removes existing structures and makes the site safe to work on. <a href="/earthworks">Bulk excavation and earthworks</a> moves large volumes of material to reshape a site or form platforms. Groundworks is the constructed below-ground package between those two and the building itself.</p>

      <p>Sequencing matters most where foundations, drainage runs and service routes cross. Agreeing where the drainage falls, the soakaway, the chambers and the incoming water, electricity and gas ducts go before excavation starts is far cheaper than breaking out concrete later. The package should then end in a defined condition: trenches backfilled and compacted, covers protected, formation levels clean and a record of what is buried where, so the next trade starts without remedial work.</p>

      <div class="gw-table-scroll" role="region" aria-labelledby="stagesCaption" tabindex="0">
        <table class="cookie-table gw-table">
          <caption id="stagesCaption" class="gw-table-caption">Typical groundworks stages and what each one delivers</caption>
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th scope="col">Groundworks stage</th>
              <th scope="col">Typical work</th>
              <th scope="col">Project outcome</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            {STAGES.map(([stage, work, outcome]) => (
              <tr>
                <th scope="row">{stage}</th>
                <td>{work}</td>
                <td>{outcome}</td>
              </tr>
            ))}
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

