<section class="page-section page-section-grey">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="gw-prose">
      <h2 class="section-title">How should you choose a groundworks contractor in Surrey?</h2>
      <p class="gw-answer">{A_CHOOSE}</p>

      <ol class="gw-steps">
        <li>
          <strong>Check comparable projects.</strong> Ask for completed work that matches the project type, scale and site conditions. Restricted-access domestic foundations and a phased commercial substructure are not the same job.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Confirm the proposed scope.</strong> Establish whether excavation, drainage, foundations, service trenches, muck-away and reinstatement are included. Disposal is a common gap between two quotations that otherwise look comparable.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Verify safety and competence.</strong> Ask for current accreditations and operator qualifications and check them rather than taking a logo at face value. Surrey Contracting holds CHAS, SafeContractor, SSIP, SMAS, CITB, CSCS, NPORS and IPAF accreditations and memberships, works to project-specific risk assessments and method statements, and runs ongoing training including First Aid at Work, CSCS, CPCS / NPORS, asbestos awareness and SMSTS. See our <a href="/health-safety">health and safety standards</a>.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Review access and plant requirements.</strong> Machinery should be matched to access width, excavation depth, material volume and neighbouring properties. A machine too big for the entrance costs days; one too small for the dig costs weeks.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Confirm technical responsibility.</strong> The quotation should establish who supplies drawings, who sets levels, who approves changes and who communicates with the structural engineer and building control.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Request a written quotation.</strong> It should identify inclusions, exclusions, assumptions, programme dependencies and the information required before work can begin, so you compare scope rather than headline price.
        </li>
      </ol>

      <p class="gw-close"><a href="/contact">Send Surrey Contracting your drawings, project postcode, access information and proposed start date for an informed groundworks quotation.</a></p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

